2. TRADEMARKS, TRADE DRESS & PROPRIETARY MARKS

2.1 Lost Limb Riders™ — Trademark and Brand Protection

“Lost Limb Riders,” associated logos, insignia, designs, slogans, color combinations, and other visual representations are proprietary trademarks, service marks, branding, and trade dress claimed by Lost Limb Riders, Inc.

The use of the ™ symbol reflects a claim of trademark rights and does not represent federal trademark registration.

Unauthorized use may constitute trademark infringement, unfair competition, false designation of origin, dilution, passing off, misappropriation, or other violations under federal or state law.

Permitted Trademark Uses: Authorized representatives only, acting in an official capacity and strictly as directed by Proprietors.

Prohibited Trademark Uses:

- Any commercial or non-commercial use without prior written authorization
- Registration, attempted registration, or claim of ownership
- Incorporation into domain names, social media handles, websites, applications, or digital accounts
- Use as part of company names, organizational names, product names, service names, or other marks
- Modification, distortion, alteration, recreation, or adaptation of any kind
- Use likely to dilute, tarnish, blur, disparage, or damage the distinctive character or reputation of the brand
- Use in connection with products, services, campaigns, or organizations other than official Lost Limb Riders offerings
- Use in comparative advertising or a disparaging, misleading, or deceptive context
- Use in any jurisdiction without prior written consent

2.2 “I Can. I Will.” — Proprietary Motto and Claimed Mark

“I Can. I Will.” is a proprietary motto and claimed trademark of John Thompson.

The use of the ™ symbol reflects a claim of trademark rights and does not represent federal trademark registration.

No person may use, reproduce, market, register, claim ownership of, or incorporate the phrase into products, services, publications, campaigns, organizations, merchandise, domain names, social media accounts, or other branding without the prior express written authorization of John Thompson.

Unauthorized use may subject the user to claims available under applicable trademark, unfair competition, copyright, contract, misappropriation, or other law.

2.3 Logo Files & Brand Assets

All visual brand materials, logos, color codes, typography, design systems, templates, insignia, graphic files, and related materials are proprietary brand assets and may constitute protected trademarks, trade dress, copyrighted works, or confidential information.

Unauthorized reproduction, distribution, modification, imitation, or use is strictly prohibited.

