3. RESTRICTED ACCESS & USE LIMITATIONS

3.1 Access Grant

Access to this repository is granted solely to:

- John Thompson, on a perpetual basis
- Board members of Lost Limb Riders, Inc., during their official tenure
- Designated staff who have received executive approval
- Designated volunteers, contractors, consultants, or representatives who have received express written authorization

Except for John Thompson’s ownership access, all access is personal, non-transferable, non-exclusive, limited, conditional, and revocable at any time, with or without cause or advance notice.

3.2 Use Restrictions

Authorized users may access and use materials only for:

- Internal organizational functions
- Board governance and decision-making
- Staff operational duties within assigned scope
- Volunteer training within the assigned program
- Authorized production, administrative, charitable, or outreach activities
- Legal compliance, accounting, investigation, and audit purposes
- Other uses expressly approved in writing by Proprietors

3.3 Prohibited Uses — Absolute Ban

Unless expressly authorized in writing, users are prohibited from:

- Public disclosure, distribution, publication, or sharing
- Commercial exploitation, sale, licensing, or monetization
- Posting materials to public or unauthorized repositories, websites, platforms, servers, or networks
- Sharing through unauthorized email, messaging, cloud storage, removable media, or file-sharing services
- Copying or retaining materials beyond the authorized employment, engagement, or project period
- Creating derivative works, adaptations, translations, modifications, summaries, reproductions, or compilations
- Extracting data, code, content, strategy, designs, media, or proprietary information for external use
- Reverse engineering, decompiling, disassembling, analyzing, scraping, or attempting to reconstruct software or systems
- Using materials in competing products, services, businesses, charities, organizations, or programs
- Using materials in educational materials, training programs, presentations, courses, or instruction without written consent
- Using materials in academic publications, studies, reports, or research
- Using materials in podcasts, videos, broadcasts, interviews, documentaries, or other media
- Lending, sublicensing, assigning, selling, or transferring materials or access rights to any third party
- Using or retaining materials after termination of employment, board service, volunteer service, contract, authorization, or engagement
- Removing, obscuring, altering, or falsifying ownership, copyright, trademark, confidentiality, or attribution notices
- Claiming authorship, ownership, contribution rights, license rights, or any other proprietary interest
- Using artificial intelligence systems, machine-learning systems, automated processors, code-generation tools, content-generation tools, or external data-processing services to upload, analyze, train upon, reproduce, summarize, modify, or process repository materials without prior written approval

3.4 Repository-Specific Restrictions

Unauthorized cloning, mirroring, forking, exporting, downloading, copying, synchronizing, archiving, backing up, or reproducing this repository or any portion thereof is prohibited.

Access credentials are personal and may not be shared.

Users may not:

- Share passwords, access tokens, API keys, recovery codes, authentication devices, or repository invitations
- Add unauthorized users, collaborators, applications, bots, integrations, or deployment keys
- Create unauthorized local or remote copies
- Push repository content to another repository, server, account, or platform
- Circumvent permissions, access controls, audit logs, security measures, or branch protections
- Alter or delete records for the purpose of concealing access, copying, modification, disclosure, or misuse

Repository activity may be logged, monitored, reviewed, investigated, and audited for security, compliance, and enforcement purposes.

