5. LIABILITY, INDEMNIFICATION & DAMAGES

5.1 Available Damages and Remedies

For any breach, infringement, misappropriation, unauthorized disclosure, or unauthorized use, Proprietors reserve the right to seek every remedy available under contract, copyright, trademark, trade-secret, unfair-competition, tort, statutory, equitable, or other applicable law.

Available remedies may include:

- Actual damages
- Compensatory damages
- Disgorgement of profits
- Restitution
- Statutory damages where authorized
- Enhanced or treble damages where authorized
- Punitive or exemplary damages where authorized
- Reasonable attorney fees and litigation costs where authorized
- Investigative, forensic, remediation, and recovery expenses
- Injunctive relief
- Specific performance
- Impoundment, seizure, return, deletion, or destruction of unauthorized materials
- Any other legal or equitable remedy available

Nothing in this Agreement limits Proprietors to any single remedy.

5.2 Injunctive Relief

Users acknowledge that unauthorized access, copying, disclosure, use, or distribution may cause immediate and irreparable harm for which monetary damages alone may be inadequate.

Proprietors may seek temporary, preliminary, permanent, or other injunctive or equitable relief as permitted by law, in addition to any claim for monetary damages.

5.3 Indemnification

To the fullest extent permitted by law, users shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Proprietors and their officers, directors, employees, volunteers, agents, representatives, successors, and assigns from claims, liabilities, losses, damages, judgments, penalties, expenses, and reasonable attorney fees arising from or related to:

- The user’s breach of this Agreement
- Unauthorized access, use, copying, disclosure, alteration, or distribution
- The user’s violation of applicable law
- Third-party claims arising from the user’s conduct
- Security incidents caused or enabled by the user
- Misuse of trademarks, copyrights, trade secrets, confidential information, names, likenesses, or brand assets

5.4 No Limitation of Liability

No provision of this Agreement limits Proprietors’ recovery or remedies for:

- Trademark infringement or misuse
- Trade-secret misappropriation
- Copyright infringement
- Breach of confidentiality
- Fraud, willful misconduct, or intentional wrongdoing
- Unauthorized access or security violations
- Violations of applicable law

---

6. ENFORCEMENT & LEGAL REMEDIES

6.1 Cumulative Rights

Proprietors’ rights and remedies are cumulative. Exercise of one right or remedy does not waive, limit, or prevent the exercise of any other right or remedy.

6.2 Right to Pursue All Remedies

Proprietors reserve the right to pursue:

- Federal civil litigation
- State civil litigation
- Criminal referral to law enforcement where potentially unlawful conduct is involved
- International legal action where jurisdiction and applicable law permit
- Immediate demands for cessation, return, deletion, or destruction of materials
- Impoundment or seizure of infringing materials where authorized
- Preservation demands, subpoenas, discovery, and other lawful investigative procedures
- Expedited court proceedings
- Emergency injunctive relief
- Claims against individuals, organizations, employers, contractors, recipients, facilitators, and other responsible parties

6.3 Attorney Fees & Costs

In any enforcement action, the prevailing party shall be entitled to recover reasonable attorney fees, expert witness fees, court costs, forensic expenses, investigation expenses, and other litigation costs to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.

6.4 Limitation Periods

All claims may be pursued within the longest applicable limitation period allowed by law.

Nothing in this Agreement shortens any limitation period, waives any discovery rule, or prevents Proprietors from asserting continuing, repeated, concealed, or newly discovered violations where recognized by law.

