7. TERM & TERMINATION

7.1 Agreement Term

This Agreement becomes effective upon the user’s acceptance or authorized access and remains binding for as long as the user possesses, accesses, retains, controls, or has knowledge of protected materials.

Provisions identified as surviving termination remain effective indefinitely or for the maximum duration permitted by law.

7.2 Termination of Access

Proprietors may terminate, suspend, restrict, or modify access immediately:

- Upon notice or suspicion of any breach
- Upon termination of employment, board service, volunteer service, contract, authorization, or engagement
- Upon completion of the authorized purpose
- For security, legal, operational, or organizational reasons
- For any reason or no stated reason
- With or without advance notice

7.3 Obligations Upon Termination

Upon termination, expiration, suspension, or revocation of access, the user must:

- Immediately cease all use of materials
- Stop accessing all repositories, platforms, devices, accounts, systems, and records
- Return or permanently destroy all authorized and unauthorized copies within five business days or sooner if directed
- Delete all local, remote, cloud, cached, synchronized, archived, exported, printed, or backed-up copies
- Disable or surrender access credentials immediately
- Certify return and destruction in writing upon request
- Cooperate with transition, audit, investigation, verification, and recovery procedures
- Preserve evidence and records if litigation, investigation, or a legal hold is anticipated or pending
- Continue complying with all surviving confidentiality, intellectual-property, and non-use obligations

Failure to comply constitutes a material breach and may support immediate enforcement.

