10. SEVERABILITY & INTERPRETATION

10.1 Severability

If any provision is held invalid, unlawful, or unenforceable, that provision shall be modified or severed only to the minimum extent necessary.

All remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.

The Agreement shall be enforced to the maximum extent permitted by law while preserving Proprietors’ intended protections.

10.2 Interpretation

Headings are for convenience only and do not limit the meaning or scope of any provision.

The words “including” and “include” mean “including without limitation.”

Singular terms include the plural where appropriate, and references to persons include individuals, corporations, nonprofits, partnerships, contractors, volunteers, representatives, and other entities.

10.3 Waiver

No waiver is effective unless made in writing by an authorized representative of Proprietors.

Waiver of one breach does not waive any prior, continuing, future, or separate breach.

